<%#
  Shown instead of a draft scorecard when the confirmation link can't be opened —
  either the id names nothing (404) or the link is missing its token, or has the wrong
  one (403).

  The link used to be /populated-scorecard-beta/<sequential id> with no token at all, so
  every scorecard ever filed could be read, and confirmed, by counting up from 1. The
  token closed that; this page is what a broken or truncated link now lands on, in place
  of either a stranger's result or a 500 whose text told a captain nothing.

  Locals: notFound (boolean).
%>
<%- include('header.ejs') %>
<%- include('nav.ejs') %>

<div class="container" style="max-width:720px;text-align:left;margin:0 auto 48px">

<% if (notFound) { %>
  <h1>We can't find that scorecard</h1>
  <p class="lead">There's no scorecard with that reference.</p>
<% } else { %>
  <h1>That link isn't complete</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Confirmation links carry a code that identifies the scorecard, and this one either
    doesn't have it or has only part of it. Some email apps break long links across two
    lines, which does exactly this.
  </p>
  <p>
    Go back to the email and open the link again &mdash; or copy the whole thing,
    including everything after the question mark, into your browser's address bar.
  </p>
<% } %>

<p>
  Nothing has been lost: the result is saved as it was submitted. If the link still won't
  open, email
  <a href="mailto:stockport.badders.results@gmail.com">stockport.badders.results@gmail.com</a>
  with the two teams and the date, and it'll be confirmed for you.
</p>

<p><a class="btn btn-success" href="/results">Back to results</a></p>

</div>

<%- include('footer.ejs') %>

</body>
</html>
